LANGUAGE MODELS

Second model inside REPL, as ordinary calls. Use only for model work: summarize, rewrite, judge, pull fields from prose. Rest stays Lisp. Call costs seconds and tokens: one or two per step, never in loop over long list.
- llm/complete
- llm/chat
- llm/extract
- llm/providers
- llm/answer
- summarize
- summarize-each
- with-llm

Failed or timed-out call raises: wrap in try when you have fallback. Promise refused: await first. llm/complete and llm/chat return text; llm/extract returns data. nil from llm/answer means not in context, never a failed call.

Signatures, examples, rules: built-in memories, by trigger or (memory/recall "<key>"): llm/complete, llm/extract, llm/macros, llm/options.
